WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:23.700
[Science Blaster- DHMIS remix] (nice music matpat)

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.920
Hello internet! Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.500
Where too much watching won't make your teeth go grey. It'll make 'em FALL OUT! (OH-NO VIEWERS GET OUT OF HERE

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.860
You might not know about this about me, but one of my favourite entertainment genres

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.380
is puppet psychological horror that comments on the state of modern children's

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.480
programming... I have very specific tastes.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.835
So, it'll come as no surprise that I am thrilled

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.520
that Don't Hug Me I'm Scared is coming back

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.215
for more

00:00:47.215 --> 00:00:48.575
Now if you're not familiar with DHMIS

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:50.535
The show is a six part series that

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.775
felt a lot like BlumHouse got a hold of

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.785
Sesame Street.(Oh no! they took my childhood!) Or the muppets just got a wee bit too

00:00:55.785 --> 00:00:58.600
sick of being so good and wholesome all the time and went

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.700
all american psycho.(like the the movie pyscho?) After this series "allegedly concluded"

00:01:01.705 --> 00:01:04.115
I did two part theory trying to unravel the messages

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:06.275
of the series while also piecing together the

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.375
lore within the show itself. And that's where things ended

00:01:09.565 --> 00:01:12.515
two years ago. With DHMIS (relegated) to the

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:15.025
archives YouTube where would live in (infamy)

00:01:15.025 --> 00:01:18.205
joining the ranks of Marble Hornets and Salad Fingers as

00:01:18.205 --> 00:01:21.245
Twisted web series that would deliver creepy nostalgia for a

00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:24.115
generation of youngsters, at least that's

00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:26.955
what I thought. Then, out of nowhere the channel

00:01:26.955 --> 00:01:29.895
suddenly became active again, dropping a new trailer entitled

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.240
"Wakey Wakey" to announce that the show was coming back

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.980
"Great! Great news!" (no pun included)

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.580
When? It's unclear.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.420
Where can we watch it? Also unclear.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.860
Maybe YouTube? But given it's now got the backing of Conaco the Production

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:45.680
company for Conan O' Bryan's show (never heard that show)it's really

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.760
anybody's guess. What's the show gonna be about? Now

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.700
that I think I can answer. Sure, the trailer left a lot

00:01:51.705 --> 00:01:53.100
people asking themselves,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.900
"I wonder what will happen.." (Me too red guy)

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.400
and it IS only 20 seconds of footage

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.800
"That's not enough time!" (SHUT IT)

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.300
But it's more than enough. Based on the trailer I'm fairly confident

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.700
I cannot only tell you the narrative arc of these episodes, but also what the deeper meaning of it all is

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.085
You see, it's my theory to that this new season is gonna be about the current

00:02:11.085 --> 00:02:13.100
political situation in America, and

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.055
The duck is Donald Trump. And if that's sounds crazy (DONALD IS HIDING EVERYONE RUN!!!)

00:02:16.055 --> 00:02:19.155
remember that this is a show where a boy wanders off from a picnic

00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:22.435
and almost ends up in a cult that worships a God who eats gravel

00:02:22.525 --> 00:02:25.265
So it's time to pick apart the trailer and see just

00:02:25.265 --> 00:02:27.695
how deep this Rabbit hole goes. To put

00:02:27.695 --> 00:02:30.185
"Wakey Wakey" into as much context as i can, let's

00:02:30.185 --> 00:02:33.235
do a quick recap of the originals six episodes and my theory for what

00:02:33.235 --> 00:02:35.635
was really going on. Don't Hug Me I'm Scared

00:02:35.635 --> 00:02:38.895
follows three main characters. The red guy, the yellow guy and the

00:02:38.895 --> 00:02:41.825
duck on a children's TV program that the red guy created and

00:02:41.825 --> 00:02:44.815
that all of them star in. The show is being corrupted by the

00:02:44.815 --> 00:02:46.175
show's producer, financier

00:02:46.175 --> 00:02:49.115
yellow guy's creepy stage dad, Roy

00:02:49.115 --> 00:02:52.125
"My dad is a com-com-computer"

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:55.065
Who's goal seems to be sell products and torture his son

00:02:55.065 --> 00:02:57.875
both of which seem to be the main messages of DHMIS as a

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.500
whole. The harmful effects that money and

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.100
advertising can have on art

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.900
and the corruption of children's programming by that kind of

00:03:03.905 --> 00:03:05.595
for profit agenda. after

00:03:05.595 --> 00:03:08.435
Red guy discovers that their show can be made cheaply and distributed onto computers

00:03:08.435 --> 00:03:11.385
his head literally explodes as he sees a way

00:03:11.385 --> 00:03:14.095
foward without the influence of Roy the Duck

00:03:14.095 --> 00:03:17.365
similary gets tired of and consumed by the show the latter again

00:03:17.365 --> 00:03:20.385
quite literaly before the red guy discovers the harmful

00:03:20.385 --> 00:03:23.345
effects that it's having on kids Yellow guy included. He

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:26.355
pulls the plug on the show and the final scene of the final episode reveals

00:03:26.355 --> 00:03:29.705
that they're moving forward with a lower budget independent reboot

00:03:29.705 --> 00:03:32.985
of the first ever episode, so that's where we're coming from

00:03:33.075 --> 00:03:35.165
now cut to "Wakey Wakey"

00:03:35.165 --> 00:03:38.205
where we get an establishing shot of "Clayhill" the town where it seems

00:03:38.205 --> 00:03:40.485
these characters live outside of the context of the show

00:03:40.485 --> 00:03:43.485
we get a quick shot of Red Guy walking through the Forrest followed by

00:03:43.485 --> 00:03:46.445
what looks like a classic episode of their usual show with the key

00:03:46.445 --> 00:03:47.775
as a teacher

00:03:47.775 --> 00:03:50.745
We get a couple of shots of computer machinery with the Ducks face on it

00:03:50.745 --> 00:03:53.715
Then, see a snapshot of a dark room in a state of disarray

00:03:53.715 --> 00:03:56.855
and the Ducks face on a large screen behind the now locked gates

00:03:56.855 --> 00:03:59.475
of Clayhill. Then, we have got ourselves a psychedelic

00:03:59.475 --> 00:04:02.475
door and a shot of a purple marble. I don't know.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.525
A lot of people online think this looks like South Parks

00:04:04.525 --> 00:04:07.805
member berries

00:04:07.985 --> 00:04:13.565
It would be a weird reference for them to make. Anyway,Wakey Wakey ends simple with Don't Hug Me I'm Scared.

00:04:13.565 --> 00:04:18.400
And then the production companies. Blink industries, Conaco, and Super Deluxe.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.615
It's not a ton to go off of, but if you actually slow it down,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.740
Pay attention to the details, and think about who's actually making this show.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.420
Some really solid narrative possibilities start to develop.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.140
First and Foremost, it's important to note that the room

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.480
That is partially destroyed in the trailer is,

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.340
On closer inspection, the office of Clayhill's Mayor.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.235
As we can see by the picture of him on the wall

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.160
And the identifying medal in the picture, on his desk. (Also the name plate on the desk)

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.120
Something happened to the mayor of this town.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.880
Notice also it's discovered by the duck.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.540
See this shot of him opening the doors, and this duck-billed shadow

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.780
When we're actually presented with the room.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.280
This is going to be important later on. The disappearance or even murder

